From c88bc17c7d7d686191e156d410a3137937c8404e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Amir <gilaniamirhossein@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 14:45:27 +0330
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] windows + fix: ws parser buffered-frames bug;
 RVPN_TLS_ROOT_CA extra roots
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- MinimalWsReader::next_frame now parses the read buffer BEFORE reading
  more bytes. Previously, when one TCP segment delivered several frames
  (e.g. a data batch right behind the server's keepalive ping), the
  frames after the first were stuck: the parser waited for a new segment
  (or reported EOF) instead of returning the already-buffered frames.
  This stalled the downlink permanently in the field. Reproduced by a
  new unit test (binary/ping/binary in one segment, then EOF).
- rvpn-tls (rustls backend): optional RVPN_TLS_ROOT_CA=path env adds
  extra PEM roots — for self-hosted deployments terminating TLS with a
  private CA or direct-IP self-signed certs (no public CA issues bare-IP
  certificates). deps: rustls-pemfile behind the rustls feature.
